{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"e09521acf70b83e5f9bc1204a5861fc9415608349fec53626d116bcb7abe412f","digest":{"component_or_area":"audit web server and CLI subcommand","key_entities":["rebar audit serve","[ui] enabled","nava-rebar[ui]","UiConfig","src/rebar/_config_schema.py","src/rebar/config.py","src/rebar/audit/server.py","src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py","src/rebar/_cli/help/audit.txt","rebar.audit.read.audit_trail","rebar.audit.server","127.0.0.1","port 8765","fastapi","uvicorn","jinja2"],"problem_keywords":["audit ui","web server","scaffolding","optional extra","config gating","lazy imports","loopback binding","read-only surface"],"propositions":["A new optional `[ui]` config section with an `enabled` flag (default false) must be wired into the config schema, coercers, and re-exports without breaking the absent-section case.","The `rebar audit serve` subcommand must not import web dependencies when the `[ui] enabled` flag is false or the `nava-rebar[ui]` extra is absent, and must exit with a friendly error message naming the flag or extra.","The server must bind to 127.0.0.1 by default, warn to stderr when `--host` is set to a non-loopback address, and support a `--port` argument (default 8765).","An index page must enumerate tickets with audit data by checking each ticket's `audit_trail()` for non-empty plan_reviews, code_reviews, or completion fields.","A live end-to-end test must seed a ticket with audit data, start the server on an ephemeral port, and assert the index page returns HTTP 200 and lists that ticket."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785822356494428847,"uuid":"89d2aa56-27ea-4b43-bfec-8aa6ed8fc6ec"}